  "title": "Mother's side",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "On your **mother's side**:\n\n- **নানা / নানি** — grandfather / grandmother\n- **মামা / মামি** — mother's brother / his wife\n- **খালা / খালু** — mother's sister / her husband\n\n'Mother's' is **মায়ের** (*mayer*). After most vowels the possessive is -র (বাবা → বাবার), but some short words take **-এর** with a little **য়** glide: মা → মায়ের, ভাই → ভাইয়ের.\n\n**মামা** is a special word: in Bangladesh it's also how you cheerfully address a rickshaw-wallah or the man at the tea stall — *Mama, ek kap cha!* You'll practise that in Lesson 6.\n\nKolkata: maternal grandparents are দাদু / দিদিমা, mother's sister is মাসি, her husband মেসো.",
